---
// Step 6: controls bound to the code in the playground (see learn/playground.ts, `data-control`).
---

<div class="learn-controls">
  <label class="wide">
    <span>System prompt</span>
    <textarea data-control="system" rows="2"></textarea>
  </label>
  <label>
    <span>Max steps</span>
    <input type="number" min="1" max="50" data-control="maxSteps" />
    <small>Model calls allowed per run. Without tools you only ever use one.</small>
  </label>
  <label>
    <span>Budget tokens</span>
    <input type="number" min="1" step="100" data-control="budgetTokens" />
    <small>How much context memory may send per request.</small>
  </label>
  <label class="check">
    <input type="checkbox" data-control="streaming" />
    <span>Stream the reply</span>
  </label>
</div>
<p class="learn-note" data-controls-note hidden>
  A control is greyed out when its line is missing from your code. Press Reset code in the Code tab to bring it back.
</p>
